`PI Stand Alone Server/Monitor Help
 This window shows all users who are logged in to the server, and
 various data associated with their respective sessions.  The data for
 each user may span up to two lines on the display.
 The first line is always displayed.  It shows the same data that is
 displayed in the System Activity display in NET.
 The second line is displayed only if the |F2| key (Display Filenames)
 has been pressed or if the |SHOW_FILES| switch has been specified on
 the command line.  It shows the number of minutes before the user will
 be forced to log off the server (if any limit is imposed), followed
 by the pathname associated with the user's most recent file operation.
 Server performance will be slightly enhanced by leaving the pathname
 display set to OFF.

 The information displayed on the first line is:

 ID#       This is the user's session identification number.  It consists
           of the low-order adapter number on which the user logged in
           and the two-byte session number.
 Username  The account with which the user logged in to the server.  If
           the username is '?' the user is in the process of logging in.
 Machine   The network computer from which the user logged in.
 Command   The last command entered.  The commands are:

   AUDIT ENTRY      A user audit entry was created.
   CANCEL SHUTDOWN  A server shutdown sequence was cancelled.
   CHANGE PASSWORD  A user changed his or her password.
   CHANGE USERNAME  A user changed his or her username.
   CLOSE FILE       A file has been closed.
   COMMIT FILE      File data has been committed to disk.
   CONTROL QUEUE    A queue entry was modified, or the despooler
                    was controlled.
   COPY FILE        A file copy was requested on the server.
   CREATE DIR       A directory has been created.
   CREATE FILE      A file has been created, or an existing file
                    with the same name may have been overwritten.
   CREATE INDIRECT  An indirect file was created.
   CREATE NEW FILE  A new file has been created.
   DELETE DIR       A directory has been deleted.
   DELETE FILE      A file has been deleted.
   DISABLE ACCOUNT  An account was disabled.
   FILE READ        Data has been read.
   FILE WRITE       Data has been written.
   FIND DISK SPACE  A user requested information about the
                    amount of free disk space.
   FIND FIRST FILE  A Find First operation was performed.
   FIND NEXT FILE   A Find Next operation was performed.
   FLUSH CACHE      The server's caches were flushed.
   FULL ACCOUNT     Account and ACL Group rights information retrieved.
   GET ACCOUNT      Account information was requested.
   GET INDIRECT     The contents of an indirect file were retrieved.
   GET LINK INFO    A user requested information about a
                    directory/device Access Control List.
   GET QUEUE ENTRY  Queue entry information was requested.
   GET QUEUE INDEX  Queue index information was requested.
   GET SERVER TIME  The current server time was requested.
   GET STREAM       A user requested information about a logical
                    printer stream.
   GET USERNAME     A username was retrieved from the account file.
   LOCK RANGE       A file region has been locked.
   LOGIN            The user is in the process of logging in.
   MULTI-MODE OPEN  A multi-mode file open was performed.
   NOTIFY OPERATER  User received an operator notification message.
   OPEN FILE        A file has been opened.
   PRINTER FIELDS   User requested printer fields from a resource.
   PRINTER STATUS   Current printer status was requested.
   REMOTE DSPL REG  Remote despooler registered.
   REMOTE DSPL DRG  Remote despooler registration cancelled.
   REMOTE DSPL IDX  Set remote despooler index.
   REMOTE Q CNTRL   Remote despooler queue control.
   RENAME FILE      A file has been renamed.
   RUN COMMAND      A remote keystroke command string was submitted.
   SEEK POSITION    A File Seek operation was performed.
   SERVER CONTROL   Server control parameters were retrieved or set.
   SET ATTRIBUTE    A file's attributes have been changed.
   SET QUEUE ENTRY  Detailed queue entry information was modified.
   SET REMOTE BLK   Set remote device block fields.
   SET STREAM       Stream information was modified.
   SHUTDOWN         A server shutdown sequence was initiated.
   TERMINATE        The user exited a program.
   TERMINATE USER   A user's access was terminated by operator request.
   TRANSLATE PATH   A network pathname was translated.
   UNIQUE FILE      A new file has been created with a unique name.
   UNLOCK RANGE     A file region has been unlocked.
   UPDATE LOGIN     Update last date of log-in in accounts file.
   USER STATUS      User status information was obtained.
   WRITE W/COMMIT   Data has been written and committed to disk.
   X GET QUEUE      Extended queue entry information was retrieved.
   X PRINT STATUS   Get extended printer status.
   X SET QUEUE      Extended queue entry information was modified.

 IOBytes    This represents the amount of data input and output that the
            server has performed for the user.  This number may be followed
            by a K, M or G, indicating kilobytes (1024 bytes), megabytes or
            gigabytes, respectively.

 #Reqs      This shows the number of requests a user has issued to the
            server since logging in.

 Privs      This shows the user's privileges for this server.  The possible
            privileges are:

    A - Super ACL Privilege
        The server will perform all of this user's requests without checking
        any ACL rights.
    Q - Super Queue Privilege
        The user can control the despooler and all printer queue entries.
        If this privilege is disabled, the user can only see and control
        their own print jobs.
    M - Super Mail Privilege
        The user can control any item in the server's mail queue.  If this
        privilege is disabled, the user can only manipulate mail items sent
        to him or sent by him.
    U - User Auditing Privilege
        The user can issue NET AUDIT commands and create audit entries in
        the server audit log.  If this privilege is disabled, user audit
        entries may not be created.
    S - System Manager Privilege
        The user can perform management functions such as issuing NET RUN
        commands and scheduling server shutdowns.
    O - Operator Notification  
        The user receives messages requesting operator action, for example,
        "out of paper" notification from printers.
    D - Remote Despooler  
        The user is able to remove print jobs from the server's printer
        queue using the remote despooler TSR program provided with
        LANtastic.
    L - Logged In
        The user is fully logged in to the server.  If the "L" is not
        displayed, the user is in the process of logging in.
    R - Remote Boot Log-in
        The user is logging in through the remote boot process.
`UI User Information Help
 This window displays all open files and record locks for the selected
 user.  The top section shows the same user attributes and statistics from
 the previous window. Note that the ID# from the previous screen has been
 split into the two following fields:

    Adapter         The adapter number of the server through which
                    the user logged in.
    Session         The user's session number on the server.
 
 The bottom section is displayed if the DOS SHARE program has been started.
 It shows information about the files that the selected user has open, and
 the record locks within each file.  An explanation of each field is shown
 below:

    Mode            Shows the file-access and file-sharing mode used to open
                    the file.  The file-access modes are Read-only, Write-only,
                    or Read/Write.  Valid file-sharing mode is the file-access
                    granted to other processes on subsequent opens.
                    File-sharing modes are Compatibility, Deny-Read, Deny-Write,
                    Deny-Read/Write, or Deny-None.
    Position        Shows the current position in the file.
    Size            Shows the size of the file.
    Lock Start/End  Shows the position of a record lock in the file.
                    There may be zero or more locks on a single file.
`PW Keyboard Lock Password Help
  Enter a password from 0-15 characters in length.  This password is then
  required to exit ALONE.  Also, CTRL+ALT+DEL is disabled while the password
  is in effect.  This allows the server to be protected from unauthorized
  access.
`CE Critical Error Help
 |Retry the Network, Disk or Device operation
  Will attempt the operation again.  First, check whether a floppy disk
  drive door is open or if some other minor problem caused the error.
  If so, correct the problem and retry the operation.
~01 |Fail the Network, Disk or Device operation
  Will cancel the operation in progress and return to the last window.
  You should then correct any problems or type Esc to exit the window.
~02 |Ignore the error, continue with program
  The program will continue as though nothing happened.  NOTE: The
  operation will NOT be properly completed and may lead to future errors.
  It is suggested that you not select this option.
~03 |Abort ALONE and return to DOS immediately
  Will exit the program immediately.
`ZZ Start of ALONE command line help
